{
  "slug": "regular-expressions",
  "title": "Regular Expressions",
  "tags": [
    "field/cs",
    "subject/automata",
    "concept/4.1/regular"
  ],
  "htmlContent": "<p>Regular expressions are symbols that allow us to define a language without using complicated and sometimes verbose symbols and notations.</p>\n<p>The main notations we will use to generate regular expressions will be the <a href=\"/notes/kleenes-and-positive-closure\">two closures we have already studied</a>. We know the Kleene's closure denotes an infinite set starting with a null and a Positive Closure simply doesn't have the null string.</p>\n<p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href=\"/notes/introduction-to-computer-theorypdf\">Defining a language associated with any regular expression (too lazy to write down)</a></p>\n<p>The best way to understand regular expressions is just by doing examples. We already know what notation we will use. There is now a new concept that we need to understand.</p>\n<p><strong>e.g1.</strong> Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\{aa, aba, abba ,abbba, abbbba ...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aba</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abba</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abbba</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abbbba</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>For this example, the regular expression would be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ab^*a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span></span></span></span>  which means a string starting with a, having an infinite amount of bs and then ending with an a as well.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>e.g2.</strong>  <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">≠</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a^*b^* \\ne (ab)^*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mord vbox\"><span class=\"thinbox\"><span class=\"rlap\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"></span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The first RE creates the set <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo>∧</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\{\\wedge, a, b, aa, bb, ab, aaa, aab, abb, bbb...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">∧</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aaa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bbb</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li>The second RE creates the set <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo>∧</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\{\\wedge, ab, abab, ababab, abababab...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">∧</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ababab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abababab</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>e.g3.</strong> Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T = \\{a,c,ab,cb,abb,cbb,abbb,cbbb...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abbb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bbb</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>In a set like this, we can deduce that each word needs to start with either a or c, followed by an infinite number of bs. The RE for this kind of a set would be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a+c)b^*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> where the operands behind and front of the + symbol means \"either a or c\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>e.g4.</strong> Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T = \\{aaa,aab,aba,abb,baa,bab,bba,bbb\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aaa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aba</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">baa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bab</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bba</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bbb</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Again, a simple deduction would lead us to conclude that this finite set can either start with a or b, have either a or b in the middle, and end with either a or b</li>\n<li>Therefore, the RE would be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a+b)(a+b)(a+b) \\equiv (a+b)^3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≡</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>e.g5.</strong> These two examples are really neat. Should be read from the book <a href=\"/notes/introduction-to-computer-theorypdf\">here</a> onwards for a complete and better understanding.</p>\n<p>We can also find <strong>equivalent expressions</strong> which define the same language in different ways.</p>\n<p><strong>e.g6.</strong> language <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≡</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">((a+b)^*a(a+b)^*a(a+b)^* \\equiv</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\